<!-- FAQs -->
<div class="section">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="section-ey">FAQs</div>
    <div class="section-h2">Common questions.</div>
    <div class="faq-list">

      <div class="faq-item">
        <div class="faq-q">Do you need access to the product to document it? <svg class="faq-chevron" width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2"><polyline points="6 9 12 15 18 9"/></svg></div>
        <div class="faq-a">Yes, and we prefer it. We test the product ourselves before writing a single word. This is how we catch inaccuracies, understand real user flows, and produce documentation that actually reflects how the product works. If direct access isn't possible, we work with your SMEs closely.</div>
      </div>

      <div class="faq-item">
        <div class="faq-q">Can you work with our existing style guide? <svg class="faq-chevron" width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2"><polyline points="6 9 12 15 18 9"/></svg></div>
        <div class="faq-a">Absolutely. If you have a style guide, we follow it to the letter. If you don't have one, we'll create one for you as part of the engagement, so every document that follows is consistent, even if someone else writes it.</div>
      </div>

      <div class="faq-item">
        <div class="faq-q">How long does a typical documentation project take? <svg class="faq-chevron" width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2"><polyline points="6 9 12 15 18 9"/></svg></div>
        <div class="faq-a">It depends on the scope. A single user guide can take 1-2 weeks. A full documentation suite for a complex enterprise product can take 6-12 weeks. We scope every project clearly upfront so you know exactly what to expect before we start.</div>
      </div>

      <div class="faq-item">
        <div class="faq-q">What if our product changes after documentation is delivered? <svg class="faq-chevron" width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2"><polyline points="6 9 12 15 18 9"/></svg></div>
        <div class="faq-a">We offer ongoing retainer arrangements for teams with frequent product updates. Alternatively, we can structure the project to include a maintenance window after delivery. We also set up documentation in a way that makes future updates straightforward for your team.</div>
      </div>

      <div class="faq-item">
        <div class="faq-q">Do you work on a fixed price or time &amp; materials basis? <svg class="faq-chevron" width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2"><polyline points="6 9 12 15 18 9"/></svg></div>
        <div class="faq-a">We work on a fixed scope, fixed price basis for most projects. This means no billing surprises, you know exactly what you're paying before we begin. For ongoing or evolving engagements, we offer monthly retainer arrangements.</div>
      </div>

      <div class="faq-item">
        <div class="faq-q">Can you document a product that is still in development? <svg class="faq-chevron" width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2"><polyline points="6 9 12 15 18 9"/></svg></div>
        <div class="faq-a">Yes. We often start documentation during the development phase, working alongside your engineering team. This approach means documentation is ready the moment the product ships, not weeks after.</div>
      </div>

    </div>
  </div>
</div>

